        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(auto-reply): honour abortSignal in human-delay sleep and wire turn signal",
        "body": "\n## Summary\nAdd `abortSignal` to `ReplyDispatcherOptions` and honour it during the human-delay sleep between block replies so an aborted turn does not wait out the full delay.\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n`createReplyDispatcher` in `src/auto-reply/reply/reply-dispatcher.ts` adds a human-like delay between consecutive block replies for natural rhythm. The delay uses `sleep(delayMs)` which does not accept an `AbortSignal` — if the turn is aborted during the delay, the dispatcher still waits the full delay before continuing, wasting time and delaying the abort path.\n\n**Code evidence**: [reply-dispatcher.ts:457](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/blob/main/src/auto-reply/reply/reply-dispatcher.ts#L457) — `await sleep(delayMs)` in the `.then()` chain.\n\nSame class of issue fixed in [#109805](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/109805) (auto-reply transient-HTTP retry backoff) and [#109913](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/109913) (discord 429 retry backoff).\n\n## Root Cause\n- `sleep()` from `src/utils/sleep.ts` uses bare `setTimeout(resolve, ms)` with no AbortSignal support\n- The `ReplyDispatcherOptions` type had no abort signal field, so callers could not pass one\n\n## Why This Fix\n1. Add optional `abortSignal?: AbortSignal` to `ReplyDispatcherOptions`\n2. In the human-delay path: check `signal?.aborted` before sleeping (early exit)\n3. If signal is present, use an abort-aware `new Promise` that clears the timer on abort\n4. If signal is absent, fall back to the original `sleep(delayMs)` — fully backward compatible\n\nOn abort, `resolve()` is used (not `reject()`) because the human delay is cosmetic — cancelling it should continue delivery, matching the pattern from `waitForReplyDispatcherIdle` in the same file.\n\n## User Impact\n- **Before**: Turn abort during human delay → waits full delay (up to 2500ms) before delivery continues\n- **After**: Turn abort during human delay → ~1ms return, delivery continues immediately\n\n## Evidence\n- Real `AbortController`, wall-clock timers, production `createReplyDispatcher` path\n- Before: abort at 200ms → still waits 1502ms → **FAIL**\n- After: abort at 200ms → returns at 202ms → **PASS**\n\n## Real Behavior Proof\n\n### Before (on main)\n\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof-reply-dispatcher-abort.mjs\nNo signal: 1508ms (expected ~1500ms), deliveries=2\nAborted @200ms: 1502ms (expected < 500ms), deliveries=2\nFAIL: abort signal ignored — waited 1502ms despite abort at 200ms\n```\n\n### After (with fix)\n\n```bash\n$ node --import tsx scripts/proof-reply-dispatcher-abort.mjs\nNo signal: 1510ms (expected ~1500ms), deliveries=2\nAborted @200ms: 202ms (expected < 500ms), deliveries=2\nPASS: abort signal honoured — delivery completed near-instantly after abort\n```\n\n## Tests and Validation\n- `git diff --check` clean\n",
        "branch": "fix/tts-contract-fetch-timeout",
